5,1,1,talk,Kenji,,Hi everyone! Let's find a way to fix the bins that makes everyone happy so we can all get along again. What should we check first?,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Shizue,,It is lovely to see you all. I wonder how other neighborhoods manage their mornings? It would be nice to know what it's actually like for the residents.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Asuka,,We need to be realistic about the labor involved. I want to know the actual time commitment for maintenance and the administrative requirements from the ward.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Rin,,I want to make sure it's fair! One house has always had the bins at their gate. We shouldn't just leave it like that if we want to be equal!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Servas,,"Peace begins with understanding. Let us look at the costs carefully, for we all have different burdens to carry. We must ensure the financial weight is fair for everyone.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, you're right! Maybe we should see how the station block does it? If they have a good system, maybe we can copy it and stop fighting!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Shizue,,"That sounds like a wonderful idea, Kenji. I would also like to see if there are any complaints from other points so we don't repeat the same mistakes.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, copying a system is fine, but we need the specific filing requirements. If the paperwork is too heavy, it will just fall on one person's shoulders again.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Rin,,"Exactly! And we need to know how big everyone's frontages are. If one person has a tiny yard and another has a huge one, that matters for where the bins go!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Servas,,A gentle reminder that the heart of the matter is often the purse. I suggest we look at the ledger and the subsidies to see what we can actually afford.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Kenji,,I'll look into the station block's bin house and their meeting minutes. I want to see how they talked through their problems to reach an agreement!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Shizue,,I think I will look into the supervised mornings on the next lane and the ward complaint log. I want to know how it feels to live there.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Asuka,,I will investigate the ward filing requirements and the truck arrival time. I need to calculate the actual hours of labor required for the setup and daily operation.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Rin,,I'm going to check the measurements of the five frontages and the statements at the residents' meeting! I want to see who said what about the fairness of the spot!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Servas,,I shall examine the block ledger of refuse-point expenses and the ward subsidy and last year's shelter costs. Let us see the truth of our spending.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
