34,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,I found out that the station block's bin house actually caused more arguments over cleaning and repairs! Maybe a fancy building isn't the best for our friendship.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh dear, that is a shame. I saw that the next lane spends quite a bit of time supervising, and our own point has had many complaints from the neighbor next to the bins.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The administrative burden is significant. A permanent structure requires a site plan and four months of processing. Also, the truck arrives very early, meaning someone must be active by 7:40 AM.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that some of our frontages are way smaller than others! One person barely has any room. It's not fair to just pick a spot without looking at the size!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"I have seen the numbers. We are spending quite a bit on small repairs, yet a new shelter is a heavy investment. We must be careful not to burden those with tight budgets.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if the truck comes that early, maybe we should pick a system that doesn't require someone to be there every single morning? That would be less stressful.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Kenji. If we make it a chore, people will be unhappy. I worry that a strict rotation might just make everyone resent the morning routine.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Precisely. If we choose a high-maintenance option, the labor will inevitably fall on the person who is most ""available,"" which is an unsustainable and unfair distribution of work.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, but if we don't have a rotation, the same person will always have the bins at their gate! That's what I'm worried about. We need a real plan for moving them!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that money and time are both forms of energy. If we spend too much of either, we lose the harmony we are trying to build. Simplicity is often the greatest kindness.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"What if we choose something that is easy to maintain and doesn't cost too much? That way, nobody feels like they are being cheated or overworked.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,That sounds very peaceful. I just hope we don't create a situation where the bins are an eyesore for someone else. We should be mindful of the atmosphere.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We must prioritize an option that minimizes the ""hidden"" labor—the filing, the early morning coordination, and the constant monitoring. Efficiency is the only way to ensure fairness.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I just want to make sure that if we say ""everyone shares,"" we actually mean it. No more ""quietly leaving it"" at one person's house for years and years!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Indeed. A fair share is not always an equal share, but it must be a sustainable one. Let us look for a path that respects both the wallet and the spirit.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
