60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried Option A will lead to fights over cleaning, like at the station block. Option B seems like it could be a lot of moving, but it's fair!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Option B sounds a bit chaotic for the neighborhood's peace. Option C seems too strict. Perhaps Option A is best if we can agree on a simple cleaning schedule?,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is a nightmare of paperwork and a four-month wait. Option C requires early morning labor that will inevitably fall on one person. Option B is the most logically efficient.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A just leaves the bins at the same house forever! That's exactly what I don't want! Option B is the only one where everyone actually takes a turn!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option A carries a heavy financial burden that may be too much for some of our neighbors. Option B costs nothing but a little effort. Let us choose the path of least financial stress.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, if we do Option B, do you think people will be happy to move the bins? I just want us to be able to talk to each other without being angry.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,I worry that moving the bins every few months will just create a new annoyance for a different person. But perhaps it is better than one person suffering forever.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, the ""annoyance"" of moving a bin is far less than the administrative burden of Option A or the daily time-sink of Option C. Option B is the only sustainable choice.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"It's not an annoyance, it's being fair! If we all take a turn, then nobody can complain that they are the only ones dealing with the smell or the mess!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"When we share the burden, the load becomes lighter for everyone. Option B allows us to maintain our friendship without asking anyone to pay more than they can afford.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I think I agree with Option B. It's the most fair, and if we all do it together, it might actually help us start talking to each other again!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"If you all feel strongly about it, I will support it. I just hope we can do it with kindness and help each other when it's time to move the bins.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is the only choice that avoids creating a permanent ""administrative victim"" or a daily labor trap. It is the most logical way to distribute the cost of the system.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! Option B is the only one that actually fixes the problem of one house doing everything. I'm definitely voting for the rotation!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a wise choice. By rotating the location, we rotate the responsibility and the cost, ensuring that no one is left behind or overwhelmed.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
